<p>
  Donations and membership fees to <%= trust.name %> are voluntary
  contributions to charitable work. This policy explains when a refund is possible.
</p>

<h2>1. General rule</h2>
<p>
  Once a donation or membership fee is received, it is used for the Trust's
  charitable work and is generally <strong>not refundable</strong>.
</p>

<h2>2. When we will refund</h2>
<p>We will refund the amount in full if:</p>
<ul>
  <li>you were charged twice for the same payment (duplicate transaction);</li>
  <li>a wrong amount was charged because of a technical error;</li>
  <li>money was deducted but the payment failed and no receipt was issued;</li>
  <li>the payment was made without your permission (for example, fraudulent card use).</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Seva on a chosen date</h2>
<p>
  If you gave for a seva on a particular date (for example, meals at Anand Dham)
  and we cannot do it on that date, we will tell you and do it on the nearest
  date you agree to. If no date suits you, you can ask for a refund within 15
  days of our message.
</p>

<h2>4. Where a cause cannot use the money</h2>
<p>
  If a cause you gave to cannot use your donation (for example, a drive is
  cancelled), we will ask you whether to move it to another cause or refund it.
  Temple Fund donations are used only for the temple and are never moved to
  another cause without your consent.
</p>

<h2>5. How to ask for a refund</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Contact us within <strong>15 days</strong> of the payment, by email or WhatsApp (details below).</li>
  <li>Give your name, transaction ID, amount, date and the reason for the refund.</li>
  <li>We may ask for proof such as a bank statement.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Processing</h2>
<ul>
  <li>We reply within 7 working days.</li>
  <li>Approved refunds are sent back to the original payment method through PayU within 7–10 working days.</li>
  <li>Any receipt or certificate issued for a refunded amount becomes invalid.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Cancellation</h2>
<p>
  A payment can be cancelled on the payment page before it is completed. After
  that, the rules above apply. Memberships cannot be cancelled for a partial
  refund. Monthly giving has nothing to cancel on the payment side, because
  nothing is debited automatically; you can stop the reminders from My Account.
</p>

